<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7031" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cătăclysmŏs</span></b> ,
			i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατακλυσμός</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A deluge</i>, <i>flood</i>, <i>inundation</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ogygi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 1, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab. 153</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Tert. Apol. 40</span></i>; Aug. Civ. Dei, 18,
			10; <i><span class="en">Lact. 2,
			20</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In medicine, <i>a pouring of water upon a diseased
				member</i>, <i>a shower-bath</i>, <i>douche</i>, <i><span class="en">Cael. Aur. Tard. 1, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 3</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
